      en: "The Semonkong Catholic Mission, established in 1880 by French Oblate missionaries, is one of the highest Catholic missions in Africa at 2,200 meters. The church's neo-Gothic architecture, built with locally quarried sandstone, features intricate stained glass windows depicting scenes from the life of Christ. The mission complex includes a primary school, a clinic, and a guesthouse that supports community-based tourism. It serves as a gateway to the Maletsunyane Falls and offers hiking trails. The mission has preserved its historical archives, including baptismal records dating back to the 19th century.",
